## Notes for sessions that can act on the repo directly

These extend AGENTS.md; they do not replace anything in it.

- **If you can run shell commands**, do the GitHub work yourself rather than printing
  instructions: create the issue, cut the branch, open the pull request, and set the
  board fields. Re-query field and option IDs every time — never reuse one from an
  earlier session.
- **If you can compact your own context or start a fresh session**, and this
  conversation has grown long, say so in the *Expected next input* line of your
  status block rather than quietly degrading.
- **If you can write files**, the session handoff goes in `{{ memoryFile }}` — see
  AGENTS.md §7. Not into an issue comment, not into a PR comment.
